# Paths under the working user's home kept in the instance's one state volume
# (mounted at ~/.persist) across rebuilds: logins and settings. One directory
# per line, relative to the home directory (a file is refused: list its
# directory); `#` starts a comment.
#
# At every container start the entrypoint makes each path a symlink into the
# volume (moving what the image put there on first use; afterwards the
# volume's copy wins). A path under one already listed is kept already; a
# parent added later is merged in on its first use. A path that no tool uses
# yet costs nothing, so the agent CLIs herdr-worktree can dispatch are listed
# ahead of time.
#
# To keep one more path in a single instance without rebuilding, add it to
# ~/.persist/persist.list inside that instance; it applies on the next start
# (the container's next start: plugins/instances/bin/instance ensure after it stopped, or rebuild).
.config     # gh, herdr and other XDG tools
.claude     # Claude Code (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR points here)
.codex      # Codex (CODEX_HOME's default)
.gemini     # Gemini and Antigravity CLIs
.pi         # pi
.local/state/nix  # Nix profiles: they must match the store in the nix volume
.cache/nix        # Nix fetcher cache (flake sources): `nix develop` skips re-unpacking
